    "q-38828": {
      "dom_id": "step-q38828",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Find all of the points where the function $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{2{x}^{2}-3x-2}$ has discontinuities due to vertical asymptotes.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the vertical asymptotes, let's start by factoring the expressions in the numerator and denominator. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{2{x}^{2}-3x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-1)(x+1)}{(2x+1)(x-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we can find the vertical asymptotes by setting the denominator to zero:\n\n$$\n(2x+1)(x-2)=0\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{1}{2},2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has discontinuities due to vertical asymptotes at $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $x=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
