    "q-340248": {
      "dom_id": "step-q340248",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "The function $f(x)=\\frac{5-x}{3{x}^{2}-10x-25}$ has a discontinuity caused by a vertical asymptote at\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the vertical asymptotes, let's start by factoring the expressions in the numerator and denominator. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{5-x}{3{x}^{2}-10x-25} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(x-5)}{(3x+5)(x-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\cancel{(x-5)}}{(3x+5)\\cancel{(x-5)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{3x+5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the vertical asymptotes, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\n3x+5=0\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{5}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has a discontinuity due to a vertical asymptote at $x=-\\frac{5}{3}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
