    "q-48247": {
      "dom_id": "step-q48247",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Find all of the points where the function $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x+2}{{x}^{2}-2x-3}$ has infinite discontinuities.",
      "worked_solution": "Infinite discontinuities coincide with the vertical asymptotes of $y=f(x).$\n\nTo find the vertical asymptotes, let's start by factoring the expressions in the numerator and denominator. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+3x+2}{{x}^{2}-2x-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+1)(x+2)}{(x+1)(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x+1)}(x+2)}{\\cancel{(x+1)}(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+2}{x-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the vertical asymptotes, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\nx-3=0\\,⟹\\,x=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has an infinite discontinuity at $x=3$ only.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
