    "q-73429": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73429",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Find all of the points where the function $f(x)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}+13x+15}{2{x}^{2}-7x-15}$ has discontinuities due to vertical asymptotes.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the vertical asymptotes, let's start by factoring the expressions in the numerator and denominator. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+13x+15}{2{x}^{2}-7x-15} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)(2x+3)}{(x-5)(2x+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+5)\\cancel{(2x+3)}}{(x-5)\\cancel{(2x+3)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+5}{x-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the vertical asymptotes, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\nx-5=0\\,⟹\\,x=5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function has a discontinuity due to a vertical asymptote at $x=5$ only.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
