    "q-340236": {
      "dom_id": "step-q340236",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "The function $f(x)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}+7x+3}{{x}^{2}+3x}$ has a discontinuity caused by a vertical asymptote at\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the vertical asymptotes, let's start by factoring the expressions in the numerator and denominator. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+7x+3}{{x}^{2}+3x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)(2x+1)}{x(x+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x+3)}(2x+1)}{x\\cancel{(x+3)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the vertical asymptotes, we set the denominator equal to zero. Therefore, the function has a discontinuity due to a vertical asymptote at $x=0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
